{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Shaphir</b> — the name of a city." "<b>ha-Ẓa'irah, in shame</b> — in exile and in captivity." "<b>Tza'anan</b> — the name of a city." "<b>did not go out</b> — to lament." "<b>the lament of Beth Ha-Etsel</b> — the name of a city. And the meaning: Beth Ha-Etsel went out to lament and not from a city to help its neighbor, for in its place it stands and takes rebuke from all these towns that are going into captivity." "<b>take</b> — learn, as in: ki leqaḥ tov (Proverbs 4:2), that it stand in its place."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:37.618310494Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}